  "pr_title": "refactor(tooling): adopt ruff, ty, and anti-slop linting",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nEnforce the coding standards with tooling and bring the existing code into compliance, so every commit is checked by the same rules.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe Python side adds `ty`, `anti-slop-python`, and `lefthook` as dev dependencies, and declares `lxml`, which the reader and patcher import directly. anti-slop-python 0.2.1 requires ruff below 0.17, so ruff moves to 0.16. The ruff configuration copies the anti-slop-python policy, so a plain `ruff check` enforces the same rules. `lefthook.yml` runs ruff, ty, anti-slop-python, pytest, and the plugin checks before each commit.\n\nAll existing findings are fixed with no exclusions or suppressions. Every function is annotated. Long functions are split by responsibility, and broad exception handlers catch specific errors. Settings from `SPSYNC_*` variables and `config.json` are read only in the new `config.py`. `reader.py`, `patch.py`, and `word.py` are now packages with the same import paths, so every module stays under the 500-line limit. A before-and-after comparison on the fixtures and a set of edits produced identical notes, patched document XML, and Word scripts. The only difference is that Word op labels and warnings now use straight quotation marks.\n\nThe plugin adds Oxlint, Oxfmt, and the anti-slop rules from dmmulroy/anti-slop at `13909c9`, plus a local `no-empty-for-loop-header` rule. `UPSTREAM.md` records the source. The configuration enables the full lint rule set. The bundle script is now `esbuild.ts`, which needs Node 23.6 or later. `main.ts` names its timing values, parses CLI JSON in one place, and drops casts that the types already cover.\n\n## Testing\n\nAutomated: `uv run lefthook run pre-commit --all-files` passes: ruff format and check, ty, anti-slop-python, 41 pytest tests, and the plugin's format check, lint, and build. The tests also pass at every commit in this branch.\n\nManual, still to do:\n\n1. Generate the fixtures with `uv run python scripts/word_fixtures.py ~/Documents/spsync-check`, open them in Word for Mac, and run `scripts/word_check.applescript`. Each document opens without a repair prompt.\n2. Copy the rebuilt `main.js` into a vault, then sync, search, and add a comment from the command palette. Each command completes and shows its result notice.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #2\n"
